gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.2756032509502607,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.2132401327175621,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":100.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.21544981735449542,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.6445448614248588,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.28035319165618744,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":-0.0013609481525438838,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":48.6,"_gate_fund_growth":0.25563530447791,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0022984195023791148,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":13.7,"_gate_share_shrink":0.013138097379618241,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":33.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.07617549379479112,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.010729999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":["paper"],"description_full":"Neurocrine Biosciences, Inc. discovers, develops, and commercialize pharmaceuticals for neurological, psychiatric, endocrine, and immunological disorders in the United States and internationally. The company's products include INGREZZA for tardive dyskinesia and chorea associated with Huntington's disease; Orilissa tablets for endometriosis; Oriahnn capsules to treat uterine fibroids; and CRENESSITY to treat congenital adrenal hyperplasia, as well as offers products under the name of ALKINDI and Efmody. Its product candidates in clinical development includes NBI-1076986 to treat movement disorders; Osavampator for inadequate response to treatment in major depressive disorder; NBI-1117568 for the treatment of schizophrenia and bipolar mania; NBI-1117567 for the treatment of Alzheimer's disease; NBI 921355 for the treatment of epilepsy; NBIP-01435 for the treatment of congenital adrenal hyperplasia; NBIP-2118 for the treatment of obesity and related metabolic diseases; and NBI-1070770 to treat major depressive disorder; and NBI-1117570, NBI-1117567, NBI-1117569, NBI-1140675, and NBI-1065890 for neuropsychiatric and neurological conditions. The company also has license and collaboration agreements with Nxera Pharma UK Limited; Takeda Pharmaceutical Company Limited; Xenon Pharmaceuticals Inc.; Voyager Therapeutics, Inc.; Sanofi S.A.; Tanabe Pharma Corporation; and AbbVie Inc. The company was incorporated in 1992 and is headquartered in San Diego, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kyle W. Gano Ph.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, improving at 29%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $299K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $87K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Neurocrine Biosciences, Inc. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $16.7B market cap on $2.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +24% over the past three years and +64% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 26% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 18-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $749M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 26 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.64\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.2%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.7pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $13.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 26% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 21% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Neurocrine Biosciences (NASDAQ:NBIX) Director Sells $44,700.00 in Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/neurocrine-biosciences-nasdaqnbix-director-sells-44700-00-in-stock.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793968180.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.896,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Neurocrine Biosciences, Inc. $NBIX Shares Sold by Sumitomo Mitsui Trust Group Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/neurocrine-biosciences-inc-nbix-shares-sold-by-sumitomo-mitsui-trust-group-inc.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793961533.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.954,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Neurocrine Biosciences (NASDAQ:NBIX) Price Target Raised to $190.00","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/neurocrine-biosciences-nasdaqnbix-price-target-raised-to-190-00.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793952067.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.727,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Neurocrine Biosciences (NASDAQ:NBIX) Stock Price Target Raised at Guggenheim","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/neurocrine-biosciences-nasdaqnbix-stock-price-target-raised-at-guggenheim.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793874412.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Contrasting Neurocri